* Start OSRM locally for Bucharest, Romania
** Download an OpenStreetMap extract for Romania (Romania does not have regions, so Bucharest alone is not available:{{wget http://download.geofabrik.de/europe/romania-latest.osm.pbf}}
** Pre-process the Bucharest (Romania) data, run each command separately
** {noformat}# 1. Extract
docker run -t -v "${PWD}:/data" ghcr.io/project-osrm/osrm-backend osrm-extract -p /opt/car.lua /data/romania-latest.osm.pbf

*# 2. Partition
docker run -t -v "${PWD}:/data" ghcr.io/project-osrm/osrm-backend osrm-partition /data/romania-latest.osrm

*# 3. Customize
docker run -t -v "${PWD}:/data" ghcr.io/project-osrm/osrm-backend osrm-customize /data/romania-latest.osrm{noformat}
** It is likely the pre-process command may fail due to docker allocated RAM. The extract command will not output any failure, but the partition command may complain that some file does not exist, see sample (with solution) [here|https://github.com/Project-OSRM/osrm-backend/issues/5689]. You need to increase the docker RAM, for Colima, follow the steps:
*** {{colima stop}}
*** {{colima start --memory <HIGER_THAN_4GB> --cpu 6 --disk 100}}
** In my case, the extract command needed 3.8 GB RAM
** Start the routing server for Bucharest:
** {{docker run -d -p 5600:5000 -v "$(pwd):/data" ghcr.io/project-osrm/osrm-backend \}}
{{  osrm-routed --algorithm mld /data/romania-latest.osrm}}
