Thanks [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] - please find responses to Lewis Silkin’s questions below.

Long story short - it looks like we responded in full back on 19 February, and Manawer missed the response. We can re-provide the data as a courtesy and flag that we already responded, which should hopefully help kill this complaint.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*(1) The date Manawer made a DSAR*
{panel}

Manawer first submitted the DSAR +_in-app_+ to Bolt Customer Support on *18 January 2025* ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/507527501] - “*Thread 1*”). Manawer asked “_How do I view all my archived chats with you guys… I cannot see all my conversations only the most recent, where are my other conversations regarding payment issues?_”

On *19 January 2025*, Manawer submitted a more formal version of the same request +_via email_+ ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/507951722] - “*Thread 2*”). Manawer asked the following: “_I am writing to formally request access to my archived chat records with Bolt regarding past conversations about my payments, deductions, and other relevant discussions… I am exercising my right to access my personal data, which includes all archived chat records, support conversations, and any related correspondence concerning my earnings and payment calculations… These records are essential for an ongoing legal matter, and I require them urgently. If any of my chat history has been deleted or removed, please provide a clear explanation of the reason for this action, along with any policies governing the retention of user support messages_.”

{color:#4c9aff}*In short*{color}: We first received the DSAR in-app on 18 January.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*(2) The date on which Bolt responded, and provided data/documents*
{panel}

Bolt Customer Support (with the support of the Privacy Team) responded +_via Thread 1_+ on 19 February 2025 ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/507527501]). The response attached unredacted copies of all of Manawer’s previous chats with Customer Support (whether in-app or via email) - I attach a copy of what was sent here: [^tickets (2) 4.json] 

* As you can see, the attachment included conversations for the period that Manawer is complaining about. We therefore responded in full on 19 January 2025.Manawer did not respond to this.

Unfortunately, it appears that Customer Support also responded separately to the same request on the same day (19 January) +_via Thread 2_+ ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/507951722]). This request contained a much more limited dataset, which Manawer has been referring to in his more recent complaints directed at Bolt.

* As such, although it is speculative, *what I think happened here is that Manawer somehow missed the response we sent him on Thread 1*. This is likely a mixture of: (i) the fact that Manawer has several Beehive threads open with Bolt simultaneously (via email and in-app); and (ii) Manawer focused pruely on the additional response sent via Thread 2, and interpreted that as the only response.

{color:#4c9aff}*In short*{color}: We responded in full on 19 February 2025. It seems that Manawer has missed our response.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*(3) Whether redacted chat transcripts were provided and if so, the basis for redactions*
{panel}

See above - What we provided on Thread 1 was not redacted. It was all Customer Support tickets with Manawer, as sourced from our data export tool.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*(4) Whether there’s been any continued correspondence with Manawer about the DSAR*
{panel}

It appears that we have not (since March) had continued correspondence with Manawer regarding this DSAR (aside from what you have already seen in the context of the currently claim). 

