Hi [~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] , thank you so much for your detailed overview of the project, the supplier, and your specific questions - it’s incredibly helpful 🙂 

In short, this solution sounds reasonable for us to proceed with, and I fully understand both the urgency and the commercial importance. I’ll make sure this is prioritized on our side.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Contract on data sharing*
{panel}

As a first and most important step, we need to ensure appropriate contractual safeguards are in place with the provider. That means signing a data processing agreement (DPA) with them. I’m attaching our DPA template, which I’ve already pre-filled with the key information. Could you please double-check Annex 1 to confirm the description of processing is accurate? Once that’s done, we can share it with the provider for their review.

This DPA is based on Bolt’s template, designed to maximize our protection and clearly allocate responsibilities in case of any privacy or security issues.

:drive: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BGYHpwTI05-cweE_mZTanRyWUDk-Fv3koPmo1OVqIEg/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BGYHpwTI05-cweE_mZTanRyWUDk-Fv3koPmo1OVqIEg/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] For review

❗ Also, I assume we should be entering into a commercial contract with them? Is it under review by [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ?

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Internal assessment - privacy team will handle*
{panel}

In parallel, as you correctly mentioned, we’re required to complete a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA). I’ll take care of that next week, but we can proceed with the agreement negotiation in the meantime.

{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
*Transparency*
{panel}

The transparency requirements are already covered in our existing privacy notices, so no additional updates are needed there.

*I will double-check if the wording is uploaded, but I already have it translated to Danish and ready to publish.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Law enforcement requests*
{panel}

One further point to note - law enforcement requests for data (including recordings) are handled centrally under our global policy to ensure compliance with data protection laws. [~accountid:618124ab3e3753006f742d1c]  from the Risk team oversees this process. Once the solution is implemented, please coordinate with her to ensure any future law enforcement requests are routed/handled correctly.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Data subject rights - aka → how do we ensure that we can give a copy of recordings to users/drivers*
{panel}

Lastly, regarding access and erasure rights: both riders and drivers have the right to request access to and deletion of their personal data. I’m looping in [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]  from our team, who manages data subject requests process across Europe, so we can align on how to operationalize this for the recordings.

For erasure, I noted that we are legally required to retain recordings for a defined retention period, and our processes will need to reflect this. 

❓ [~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] However, I’d like to clarify one point - when users request access to these recordings, will it be technically feasible to provide copies? If so, what would the process look like? [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]  and I can help shape the right approach here.

